A process composer with ordering and parallelism based on directed acyclic graphs

This command (without any other command) will attempt to spawn all processes in the selected Engage file, starting with processes without dependencies and spawning subsequent processes as their dependencies become ready. If specified, the `-p`/`--process` option will cause Engage to only attempt to spawn the selected processes and their dependencies.

Usage: engage [OPTIONS]
       engage <COMMAND>

Commands:
  completions  Print completions for a supported shell
  dot          Print a graph in Graphviz' DOT language of processes and their dependencies
  list         Print available processes
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -f, --file <FILE>
          Manually select the Engage file
          
          This option overrides the default searching behavior.

  -l, --log-format <FORMAT>
          Select the log format
          
          The `default` format is the "intended experience". The other formats are primarily useful for debugging or getting structured logs. Formats other than `default` will use the value of the `RUST_LOG` environment variable as the log filter if it's set, otherwise `info` is used.

          Possible values:
          - default: The default format
          - compact: [`tracing_subscriber`]'s compact format
          - full:    [`tracing_subscriber`]'s full format
          - pretty:  [`tracing_subscriber`]'s pretty format
          - json:    [`tracing_subscriber`]'s JSON format
          
          [default: default]

  -p, --process <PROCESS>
          Select a process
          
          This option can be specified multiple times.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
